+Why no real money is at risk:
 
-![Debug Contracts tab](https://github.com/scaffold-eth/scaffold-eth-2/assets/55535804/b237af0c-5027-4849-a5c1-2e31495cccb1)
+- The fork runs with **chain id 31337**, not 8453. Anything signed for it can't be replayed on Base (EIP-155), and wallets treat it as a separate network.
+- In dev mode the frontend targets only the local chain (`scaffold.config.ts`). Base mainnet is only targeted in the production build.
+- Test USDC is **minted on the fork** by impersonating USDC's real `masterMinter` (the same path Circle uses to mint). It moves through the real USDC contract, but only exists on your fork.
+- `yarn fund` refuses to run against any node whose chain id isn't 31337.
 
